@format 1
@id keyframes.nearest
@title Move to nearest keyframe
@area 3. Keyframes and waveform
@entry input
@summary Compare adjacent keyframes only after scan coverage in both directions proves that the nearest candidate is valid.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related keyframes.scan, keyframes.previous, keyframes.next

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias key = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LKeyframeOrchestrator

[input] Nearest-keyframe command <input>
- Dispatch the nearest-keyframe shortcut when timeline commands and a spool are active @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...)
> find

[find] Compare covered neighbours <decision>
- Resolve previous and next candidates only when their contiguous directional scan coverage is current @ key.LKeyframeNearestMove(...)
- Choose the closer proven timestamp; an equal distance chooses the previous timestamp @ key.LKeyframeNearestMove(...)
? "Both directions are covered and a candidate exists" > move
? "Both directions are covered and no candidate exists" > unavailable
? "Either direction has incomplete coverage" > scan

[move] Move to stored candidate <process>
- Accept the non-null selected candidate and propagate it as the new cursor @ flow.PFlowKeyframeMove(...)
- Update both timeline views, request a scan around the new position, and seek the preview @ flow.PFlowCursorPropagate(...)
> result

[result] Nearest keyframe selected <output>
= The cursor moves only after both directional searches are sufficiently covered for a reliable comparison.

[unavailable] No nearest keyframe <output>
= The covered search ranges contain no adjacent keyframe, so the cursor remains unchanged.

[scan] Scan around the unchanged cursor <process>
- Keep the nearest-keyframe command pending and start a focused scan immediately @ flow.PFlowKeyframeMove(...)
> wait

[wait] Re-evaluate current scan notices <process>
- Retry the pending command whenever a source-current scan notice updates keyframes and covered ranges @ flow.PFlowNoticeHandle(...)
> find
